	(text "Analog front end.\nAzimuth ends are AZ_POT_3 and AZ_POT_7 from the rotor sheet. The wiper is ROTOR_RETURN.\nEach pot end is 330 ohm from +3V3, then 1k, then a 60 Hz twin-T,\nthen 10k and 100 nF, then BAT54 clamps to +3V3 and to ground.\nTwin-T is 121k, 121k, and 60.4k, with 22n, 22n, and two 22n in parallel.\n1/(2*pi*121k*22n) is 59.8 Hz. The clamps are after the notch, so they do not clip 60 Hz first.\nThe 100 nF after 121 k ohm is about 4.7 Hz. A step is within 1 percent in about 0.16 s. Five volts peak at 60 Hz leaves about 2 mV at the ADC.\n\nJ5 is the elevation rotor cable, not a potentiometer.\nPin 1 wiper to ROTOR_RETURN, pin 2 end A, pin 3 end B. Through-hole, Mouser TBD.\nD19 and D22 are SMAJ90CA, LCSC C5353147.\nAzimuth clamps D6 and D7 stay on the rotor sheet.\nTR1 and its conditioning stay on rotor_drive. I_SENSE is only carried across to I_ADC.\nVIN_WARN is 39k over 1k into the comparator, with no capacitor."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 203.2 30.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "5035aef6-a19b-4762-99b5-fc01074d74ed")
	)
